For portfolio weights \(x\), benchmark weights \(b\), and realized returns \(r\in U\), relative performance is the active return \[R_{
rm rel}(x,b;r)=r^\top x-r^\top b=r^\top(x-b).\] The guaranteed relative performance is \(\inf_{r\in U}R_{
rm rel}(x,b;r)\). A robust relative-performance portfolio maximizes this guarantee over a feasible set \(X\): \[\max_{x\in X}\inf_{r\in U}r^\top(x-b).\] A target \(\gamma\) is robustly attained exactly when \(r^\top(x-b)\ge\gamma\) for every \(r\in U\).
